# DURABLE REPRO — D10 exclusivity hole A10: the nested-writer conflict at a
# STRUCT-CONSTRUCTOR position (`Pair(v[0], mutate(&v))`).
#
# This is the exact shape that forced the SAME-DAY AMENDMENT to D10(b)
# ADDENDUM 3 (`docs/define-gorget/decisions.md`, end of the LOG). The addendum
# first exempted owned-field ctor args from the overlap rule on the reasoning
# that "this position already clones, so the arg is a value, not a live alias".
# The GIR refutes it: the boundary clone is emitted at the `struct_init`, i.e.
# AFTER every sibling arg has been evaluated —
#   _8  = index_load _1, 0          (raw ptr into `v`)
#   _11 = borrow_mut _1
#   _12 = call @mutate(_11)         <- reallocs `v`; _8 now dangles
#   _13 = call @gorget_string_clone_to_owned(_8)   <- reads FREED memory
#   _14 = struct_init Pair { _13, _12 }
# So an owned-field ctor arg IS a live alias across sibling evaluation.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C backend, `--sanitize`): `gg check`
# clean, then AddressSanitizer heap-use-after-free in
# `gorget_string_clone_to_owned`.
#
# INTENDED: REJECTED at `gg check` with `E_BorrowConflict`. Per the corrected
# rule, an aggregate-init owned-field position is exempt on the MOVER axis only
# (`Pair(v[0], !v)` stays ACCEPTED — see
# `sound_ctor_mover_sibling_accept.gg`), and STILL PARTICIPATES against a
# sibling WRITER, because a writer can realloc before the boundary clone runs.
#
# The 4096-push loop FORCES a real reallocation.
#
#
# ORACLE (ggdef, measured this session): ACCEPTS this program and prints the
# pre-mutation value. ggdef is a definitional INTERPRETER with value semantics,
# so a reallocation cannot invalidate anything and this UAF class is
# structurally unobservable in that lane — it is NOT the authority here. The
# intended REJECT comes from the ratified D10 exclusivity ruling, which ggdef
# owes as part of the same landing (Core #9). Full note in
# `sound_excl_getchain_local.gg`.
# Cited from TODO.md (CoW / ownership / High): the D10 "one exclusive writer"
# structural-chokepoint entry (nested-writer costume, constructor sibling).
struct Pair:
    String s
    int n

int mutate(Vector[String] &v):
    int i = 0
    while i < 4096:
        v.push("filler-padding-to-force-a-real-reallocation")
        i = i + 1
    return v.len()

void main():
    Vector[String] v = Vector[String]()
    v.push("alpha-heap-forced-payload")
    Pair p = Pair(v[0], mutate(&v))
    print(p.s)
